{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "the social network is a 2010 film directed by david fincher that tells the story of the founding of facebook, the social media giant that has become an integral part of modern life. the movie is based on the book \"the accidental billionaires\" by ben mezrich, which chronicles the rise of mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook, from his harvard days to the company's early success.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard, getting dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright (played by railey mcconnell). in a fit of anger and hurt, mark creates a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two harvard students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nlater, mark is approached by twin brothers cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the harvard rowing team and are looking to create a social networking site for harvard students. mark agrees to help them, but eventually decides to create his own site, which he calls \"thefacebook\". with the help of his friend eduardo saverin (played by andrew garfield), mark launches the site, which quickly becomes a huge success.\n\nas facebook grows in popularity, mark and eduardo become embroiled in a dispute over the direction of the company and the ownership of its shares. meanwhile, the winklevoss twins claim that mark stole their idea and sue him for damages.\n\nthe film is notable for its nuanced portrayal of mark zuckerberg, who is depicted as a complex and multifaceted character. jesse eisenberg's performance is superb, capturing mark's intelligence, ambition, and awkwardness. the supporting cast is also excellent, with standout performances from andrew garfield and justin timberlake (who plays sean parker, the co-founder of napster).\n\none of the strengths of the film is its exploration of the themes of friendship, betrayal, and the consequences of ambition. the movie raises important questions about the ethics of social media and the impact it has on our lives. it also provides a fascinating glimpse into the world of tech startups and the culture of silicon valley.\n\nthe film's cinematography is also noteworthy, with a distinctive visual style that captures the sterile, modern feel of harvard and the tech world. the score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is equally impressive, adding to the film's tense and unsettling atmosphere.\n\noverall, the social network is a thought-provoking and engaging film that is both a biography of mark zuckerberg and a commentary on the world we live in today. it is a must-see for anyone interested in technology, entrepreneurship, or the complexities of human relationships.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.9773347973823547}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -7.30726242181845e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.014163684099912643}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -9.536738616588991e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -1.7377774715423584}, {"token": "201", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0005864569102413952}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.0005529781919904053}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " that", "logprob": -0.10195189714431763}, {"token": " tells", "logprob": -0.0009837078396230936}, {"token": " the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " story", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.0132738680113107e-05}, {"token": " founding", "logprob": -3.123234637314454e-05}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0015023384